  )
  (text "Place one pair of 100 nF capacitors near the power pins of each IC"
    (at 15.24 190.5 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 46480983-3e19-461c-9ca7-69e52083ddec)
  )
  (text "Power and decoupling" (at 44.45 151.13 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 6394b892-cfc0-471f-b8a0-c1a9881265ae)
  )
  (text "Difference amp A_{v}=0.1" (at 85.09 121.92 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 77b0e5b3-3551-4298-af73-38f1054ae7ec)
  )
  (text "All resistors are 1/4 W 1% metal film except as noted.\n* - See description for the values used in the different tests.\nC2 and C3 are 25V aluminum electrolytic; all others are 50V X5R or Y7V ceramic."
    (at 176.53 146.05 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 7dfd6035-c47b-46ce-895b-a4adc52df9f3)
  )
  (text "Reference voltage" (at 27.94 139.7 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 84e93019-9904-4d47-9fda-f726a16f585a)
  )
  (text "Initial demonstration.\nLoad is a short circuit; MES2 measures output current."
    (at 161.29 170.18 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid ec5d59a3-586e-48a4-b193-c2b498c9edca)
  )
  (text "U2 is wired 'backward' with the 100k resistors (the 'sense' and 'ref' terminals)\nconnected to the input, while the 10k resistors (the '+' and '-' terminals)\nare connected to the feedback loop.\nWith R3=100 ohms, the voltage gain with respect to the input is 0.1.\nThe transconductance will be 0.1/R_{s} - or 0.001 S:  1 volt of input will yield\n1 mA of output.\n\nWe also experiment with R3=1k and R3=10k.\n\nInitially, we test with R4 shorted.\nThe load impedance is just the meter's current shunt, so the feedback\nresistor on the '-' terminal will be much greater than the load and\nthe current through it can be ignored.\n\nWe repeat tests with R4=1k.\nIn that configuration, we also try R3=10k, so that 1 volt of input will\nyield 10 µA of output, and note the failure. The failure comes about\nbecause now the current through the '-' terminal of the diff amp\nbecomes significant."
    (at 168.91 99.06 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid f3b7e491-ccda-4b49-86e1-761e6715866f)
  )

